lib — PDP-11 target runtime
===========================

The object files the linker pulls in for a PDP-11 program: the C runtime
startup and the C library.  They install to `/usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7/`.

  crt0.s  fcrt0.s  mcrt0.s  fmcrt0.s   V7 /usr/src/libc/csu sources, kept
                                       unmodified; `make` assembles them with
                                       our own `as` into the .o files.  The
                                       assembled .o are byte-identical to the
                                       V7 disk image's (verified).
  libc.a                              the prebuilt V7 C library, copied from
                                       the V7 disk image (/lib/libc.a).  It
                                       carries csv/cret/cerror, the arithmetic
                                       helpers, printf, write, exit, ...

libc.a is a stopgap: it is the *reference* library pulled off a real V7
image so linking works today, pending a from-source build of V7's
/usr/src/libc (orig -> c99 -> modern).  It is not assembled here.
